# AGENTS.md stays short

`AGENTS.md` is loaded into every agent session, so every line costs context
and long files are followed less reliably. Keep the root file under about 150
lines.

## When to add a line

Add a line only when both are true:

- An agent would get it wrong without being told (a non-obvious rule, or a trap
  that the tests do not catch).
- It is stable. It will still be true after the next few pull requests.

Write it as one short instruction with its reason. Check that it is true
against the code before you add it.

## Where everything else goes

| Content                                             | Place                                    |
| --------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| How a feature works, architecture, design rationale | Code comments or `docs/`                 |
| Setup, validation commands, pull request policy     | `CONTRIBUTING.md`                        |
| Rules for one package or area only                  | A nested `AGENTS.md` in that directory   |
| Lists of tools, settings, scripts, or files         | Nowhere. Agents read them from the code. |
| What a change did, history, status                  | The commit message or pull request       |

## When you change behavior

Remove or correct any `AGENTS.md` line that your change makes untrue. A wrong
line is worse than a missing one.
